THE SIDE-RAYS THREAD, now resolved after three moves, and the sequence is the
lesson. Same component, three positions, each one a correct fix for the
complaint in front of me and wrong for the one behind it:
  1. section + overlay (z-30)  -> painted over the photo and quote.
  2. inside the left column    -> could not reach the photo, but the light also
                                  stopped at the column boundary.
  3. section, z-0, before the  -> behind BOTH columns. 'Behind everything but
     z-10 grid                    still visible' is only satisfiable here.

What I should have noticed at step 2: I solved 'must not cross the photo' by
shrinking the element's REACH, when the actual requirement was about DEPTH.
Reach and depth are different axes; constraining the wrong one produces a fix
that passes the current test and fails the next one. When a complaint is about
what is in front of what, the answer is always the stacking order, never the
bounding box.

Line 11 closed the club-colour thread for good, and it is worth recording that
the correction was to my own over-correction: I picked rose to avoid 'evil red'
and landed so warm it read as the orange card again ('Sigma phi is same as ai
alignment'). Avoiding one failure mode by a wide margin walked straight into
the opposite one. Aim for the middle of the target, not the far edge of the
acceptable region.

Line 15 was two symptoms of one cause: rainbow experience cards ABOVE a
monochrome stack. Fixing either alone would have left the page incoherent.
Both now walk one cyan->magenta ramp from a single table, so they cannot drift.

